+# Todo Due Dates Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [x]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Add optional todo due dates, filter overdue open todos through the JSON API and a list-page button, and label them `überfällig`.
+
+**Architecture:** Keep storage and date validation in `src/store.mjs`, using a computed `overdue` value whenever a todo is returned. The HTTP handler filters these computed results and maps `ValidationError` to HTTP 400. The list renders API results using DOM text nodes and toggles between the full and filtered endpoints.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24; Node builtins only; `node:test`; existing HTML and JavaScript; Playwright MCP for browser verification.
+
+**Spec:** Small-change scope agreed in chat and posted as `Approved Spec` on Gitea ticket #1, `http://gitea:3000/adw/demo-todo/issues/1`.
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- An open todo is overdue exactly when its due date is before today in UTC; today, future, completed and undated todos are not overdue.
+- `dueDate` is a real calendar date formatted `YYYY-MM-DD`, or `null`; omission on creation defaults to `null`.
+- `PATCH` omission preserves the date; explicit `null` removes it. Return `dueDate` and boolean `overdue` for creation, update, get and list.
+- `GET /todos?overdue=true` returns only overdue todos, preserving order; absence of `overdue` or `overdue=false` returns all todos. Other values return HTTP 400. This boolean query contract is the agent's implementation choice.
+- Invalid types, formats and impossible dates throw `ValidationError`, mapping to HTTP 400. A rejected patch leaves every field unchanged.
+- Node 24, exclusively Node builtins, no additional dependencies; tests in `test/` fail before implementation.
+- Preserve the list order. Show the due date when present and the exact lowercase text `überfällig` only for overdue todos. New tested elements have `data-testid` attributes.
+- A button labelled exactly `nur überfällige` toggles filtering on and off, exposes its state with `aria-pressed`, and requests the filtered API when active. Initial state is off. Empty results render an empty list.
+- Agent browser verification covers dated, undated, overdue, today and completed todos, toggling the filter both ways and empty results; evidence stays outside the repository; stop the app afterwards.
+- Branch: `1_faelligkeitsdatum_todos`; draft PR against `main`, titled `WIP: 1: Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos`; never merge or close the ticket.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+1. JavaScript date normalization must not accept February 30 or a non-leap February 29; test invalid dates in Task 1.
+2. A rejected mixed patch must not partly change title, done or date; test a fetched unchanged record in Task 1.
+3. Reading after midnight UTC must recompute overdue without a write; test clock advancement in Task 1.
+4. A machine's local timezone must not change the UTC comparison; run Task 1's fixed-clock tests with `TZ=Pacific/Honolulu`.
+5. Filtering must exclude completed, undated and today-due records and return an empty array when appropriate; test API outcomes in Task 1 and toggle/empty UI results plus literal markup-like title text in Task 2.
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Due dates and overdue API responses
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/store.mjs`
+- Modify: `src/app.mjs`
+- Modify: `test/app.test.mjs`
+- Create: `test/store.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: `createStore()` and its existing `add`, `update`, `get`, `list` and `remove` methods; `createApp(store)` and existing HTTP routes.
+- Produces: Todo snapshots shaped `{ id: number, title: string, done: boolean, dueDate: string | null, overdue: boolean }` from `add`, `update`, `get` and each `list` entry. Missing records keep their existing behavior.
+- `add({ title, dueDate })` defaults absent dates to `null`; `update(id, patch)` validates before mutation. `overdue` is read-only derived output, never stored or accepted as authoritative input.
+- `GET /todos?overdue=true` consumes computed store snapshots and returns only records whose `overdue` is true; `false` or omission returns all; invalid query values map to HTTP 400.
+
+- [x] **Step 1: Write failing API contract tests in `test/app.test.mjs`.** Update the existing complete-object expectation to include `dueDate: null, overdue: false`. Add tests asserting POST persists `dueDate: '2026-10-20'`; GET and list return the date and boolean `overdue`; PATCH changes, preserves and removes the date; invalid inputs return 400 and a subsequent GET equals the record before the rejected patch. Include existing CRUD behavior in the suite.
+- [x] **Step 2: Write failing store tests in `test/store.test.mjs`.** Freeze Date at `2026-10-21T00:30:00.000Z` with Node's test clock. Assert `overdue` is true for an open `2026-10-20` todo and false for dates `2026-10-21`, `2026-10-22`, null and an omitted date. Assert completion removes overdue and reopening restores it. Advance from `2026-10-21T23:59:59.999Z` to `2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z` and assert GET and list change a `2026-10-21` todo from false to true without writes.
+- [x] **Step 3: Add validation cases before implementation.** Assert `ValidationError` for `''`, `'2026-2-01'`, `'2026-02-30'`, `'2025-02-29'`, timestamps, whitespace, numbers, booleans, objects and arrays; assert acceptance of `'2024-02-29'`. Exercise creation and patch validation. After a mixed valid-title/invalid-date patch and a valid-date/invalid-done patch, assert every stored field is unchanged. Verify setting an input `overdue` cannot override the derived value.
+- [x] **Step 3a: Add failing API filter tests.** With fixed UTC time or dynamically derived UTC dates, create yesterday-open, today-open, future-open, yesterday-done and undated records. Assert `?overdue=true` returns only yesterday-open, `?overdue=false` and omission return all in insertion order, completing the overdue record yields `[]`, reopening restores it, and invalid query values return 400.
+- [x] **Step 4: Run `npm test`.** Expected: new assertions fail because date fields, validation and derived overdue are absent. Confirm the failures are behavioral assertions rather than setup errors.
+- [x] **Step 5: Implement date validation and computed response snapshots in `src/store.mjs`, and the list filter in `src/app.mjs`.** Validate exact formatting and round-trip the parsed UTC calendar date; calculate today using UTC for each operation, not at store creation. Validate all patch fields before applying any. Filter on the computed `overdue` output and validate the boolean query value with `ValidationError`.
+- [x] **Step 6: Run `npm test` and `TZ=Pacific/Honolulu npm test`.** Expected: all tests pass in both environments, including the fixed UTC-midnight and atomicity cases.
+- [x] **Step 7: Commit the API/store deliverable and updated plan tracking.** Suggested message: `feat: add validated todo due dates and UTC overdue status`.
+
+### Task 2: Due dates in the list and browser verification
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `public/index.html`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: Task 1's `GET /todos` response, preserving its order and existing `todo-item` and `todo-title` test IDs.
+- Produces: A date element with `data-testid="todo-due-date"` when `dueDate` exists, a marker with `data-testid="todo-overdue"` and text `überfällig` only when `overdue` is true, and a toggle button with `data-testid="overdue-filter"`, label `nur überfällige` and boolean `aria-pressed`.
+
+- [x] **Step 1: Start the app from the implementation checkout with `PORT=3000 npm start` and wait for `/health` to return `{ "ok": true }`.** Seed through the API with dates derived from current UTC today: open yesterday, open today, open tomorrow, completed yesterday and undated. Include a title containing literal HTML-like text.
+- [x] **Step 2: Verify the missing UI behavior in Playwright before editing the page.** Open `/`; assert an overdue row contains its due date and `überfällig`, and the `nur überfällige` button exists. Expected: the UI assertions fail because these elements are missing, while Task 1's API tests already demonstrate the complete feature's failing-test-first cycle in `test/`.
+- [x] **Step 3: Extend `public/index.html`.** Append a semantic `time` element displaying the exact stored date when present; append `überfällig` with readable spacing only for overdue rows. Use `textContent` for all API-derived text, preserving existing title and done display. Add the filter toggle and reload the list from `/todos?overdue=true` when on, `/todos` when off; disable it while loading to serialize requests.
+- [x] **Step 4: Run `npm test`.** Expected: the entire test suite passes.
+- [x] **Step 5: Reload `/` with Playwright MCP and inspect rows by `data-testid`.** Assert all five cases show the correct dates, only open yesterday has lowercase `überfällig`, the done marker remains visible, and the HTML-like title is literal text. Toggle `nur überfällige` on and off and assert the network endpoint, rows and `aria-pressed`; complete the last overdue todo and assert an empty filtered list. PATCH a date and remove it via the API, reload, and verify the list updates.
+- [x] **Step 6: Save a screenshot outside the repository and stop the app.** Stop it even if verification fails; report any unavailable browser tooling or startup failure rather than claiming browser success.
+- [x] **Step 7: Commit the list deliverable and updated plan tracking.** Suggested message: `feat: display due dates and overdue todos in the list`.
+
+### Close-out
+
+- [x] Review the full branch against the agreed scope and address material findings.
+- [x] Run final required checks and inspect `git diff --check` before claiming success.
+- [x] Write the Implementation Summary, push the branch and open the draft PR with `tea` as specified in `.agents/includes/ticketing.md`.
